{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Social Computing.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Social Computing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"social computing social computing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Social Computing.md","fileName":"Social Computing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Social Computing","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Human-Computer Interaction Foundations]] · [[Conversational Assistant Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Conversational Assistant Design","Embodied Interaction","Computer-Supported Cooperative Work","Telepresence","Assistant Personality","Social Virtual Assistant","Social Robot","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","aiassistants.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Social Computing.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Social Computing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"social computing social computing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Social Computing.md","fileName":"Social Computing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Social Computing","heading":"Social Computing","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Social computing describes systems that serve as a medium or focus for social relationships. As a medium, a system supports existing social conventions and contexts. As a focus, it creates new forms of social activity that would not otherwise occur.\n\nBecause conversations and conventions are situated in social reality, social computing is a form of [[Embodied Interaction]]. It is closely related to [[Computer-Supported Cooperative Work]], which concentrates on supporting collaborative activities and their coordination.\n\nIn three-dimensional environments, social computing can place remote users in a shared virtual space through [[Telepresence]].\n\nConversational assistants can also become social actors rather than neutral communication channels. Voice, timing, memory, and [[Assistant Personality]] invite people to apply social expectations to a [[Social Virtual Assistant]] or [[Social Robot]], even when the system's actual understanding is narrow.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Conversational Assistant Design","Embodied Interaction","Computer-Supported Cooperative Work","Telepresence","Assistant Personality","Social Virtual Assistant","Social Robot","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","aiassistants.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Social Computing.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Social Computing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"social computing social computing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Social Computing.md","fileName":"Social Computing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Social Computing","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n\n[[aiassistants.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Conversational Assistant Design","Embodied Interaction","Computer-Supported Cooperative Work","Telepresence","Assistant Personality","Social Virtual Assistant","Social Robot","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","aiassistants.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}